__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env
.DS_Store
/tmp/
*.swp
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Local Claude Code settings (personal paths)
.claude/

# Baseline measurement artifacts (regenerated via extract.py --live)
tools/extractor/baseline/images/*
!tools/extractor/baseline/images/.gitkeep
tools/extractor/baseline/results*.csv

# Rust build artifacts
cli/target/

# Web app artifacts (web/.gitignore owns web/.env and its variants)
web/node_modules/
web/.svelte-kit/
web/build/

# Publish surface: `make site` assembles it from publish/ plus the tracked
# ontology, shapes and schema files. Reproducible, never edited by hand — edit
# the sources under publish/ instead.
/site/

# Markdown files — do not commit, in any subfolder.
# Existing tracked .md files (README.md, docs/vson.md, spec/*.md, etc.)
# remain tracked; this rule only blocks NEW .md from being staged.
*.md

# CONTRIBUTOR WARNING: because of the `*.md` rule above, a NEW markdown file is
# invisible to git until its exact path is negated below. If you add one and
# `git status` does not show it, that is why — add a `!path/to/file.md` line here.
#
# Normative markdown that MUST ship (loaded at runtime or referenced by
# tracked sources — see web/src/lib/server/prompt.ts and
# scripts/deploy_preflight.sh).
!docs/vson-x-semantics.md
!skills/vson-extractor-x/SKILL.md
!skills/vson-extractor-x/README.md
!tools/extractor/prompts/specialized/repair-x.md
# The byte-identical mirrors of four of the above, carried inside the crate so
# `vson mcp` works outside a checkout (cli/src/commands/embed.rs). They are
# generated — `python3 scripts/check_embedded_assets.py --sync` writes them and
# `make cli-check` proves they still equal the originals — but they must ship,
# because `include_str!` reads them at compile time.
!cli/assets/skills/vson-extractor/SKILL.md
!cli/assets/skills/vson-extractor-x/SKILL.md
!cli/assets/tools/extractor/prompts/specialized/repair.md
!cli/assets/tools/extractor/prompts/specialized/repair-x.md
# Repo-policy files GitHub surfaces from the root.
!SECURITY.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
# The competitive page. Prose, not runtime input — but every claim on it names a
# checked-in fixture and a command, and README.md links it as its second section,
# so a repository without it ships a dangling link.
!docs/why-not-json-schema.md
# The vision-dataset importers: their reference, the measured coverage study
# `make importer-check` re-derives, and the licence/attribution draft that holds
# publication of anything dataset-derived until a person has reviewed it.
!docs/importers.md
!docs/eval/coverage.md
!docs/eval/attribution.md
# The credits for the pixels the studio actually ships. It is deployed with the
# site (static/ is published verbatim), and web/tests/demo-credits.test.ts fails
# the build when it is missing or does not cover every manifest entry.
!web/static/demos/CREDITS.md
# The annotated directory tree the README carried until v1.4.0. README.md links
# it from the Docs section, so a repository without it ships a dangling link —
# and `make check`'s anchor gate fails on one.
!docs/repo-map.md
# The pull-request checklist. GitHub reads it from the repository itself — an
# untracked template is no template — and Markdown is the only form it takes;
# there is no YAML pull-request form the way there is for issues.
!.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md

# Generated eval artifacts (scripts/d_smoke_eval.sh writes here)
reports/

# Stray example images — the curated examples/ corpus is .vson/.ttl text.
examples/*.jpg
examples/*.jpeg
examples/*.png

# Local launch tooling, deliberately untracked. It prepares a one-time history
# rewrite, so it names the file that rewrite removes, that file's blob hash, the
# commit whose message it replaces, and the replacement text. Committed, it
# would ship in the public repository and sit in the rewritten history for ever
# — a searchable pointer to exactly what was withdrawn, which is the state the
# rewrite exists to end. Keep a copy outside the checkout if you want one after
# the flip.
/scripts/launch/
